          %p
            see Example
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SpinnSpin2IsSpinc"}
            below.
          %p
            %br/
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#as_the_effective_quotient_of__acting_on_
            As the effective quotient of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Sp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp(n)\times Sp(1)
            acting on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℍ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{H}^n
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+product+group"} direct product group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Sp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp(n) \times Sp(1)
            has a canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternion"} quaternion
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℍ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{H}^n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sp%28n%29"} Sp(n)
            acts as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ×
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \times n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternion+unitary+group"} quaternion unitary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrix+multiplication"} matrix multiplication
            from the left, and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp(1)
            acts by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal"} diagonal
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ×
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \times 1
            matrix action on each
            = succeed "-summand" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℍ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{H}
          %p
            For instance for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 2
            this action controls the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternionic+Hopf+fibration"} quaternionic Hopf fibration
            and its
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp(2)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+function"} equivariance
            (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "quaternionic+Hopf+fibration#EquivariantStructure"} there
          %p
            But this action is not an
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+group+action"} effective group action
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:DiagonalCenter"} (1)
            acts trivially.
          %p
            There is then a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groups"} Lie groups
          #eq:CompatibilityDiagram.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Sp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ×
                          %mi Sp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %mi Spin
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 8
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Sp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mi Sp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %mi SO
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 8
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  Sp(2) \times Sp(1)
                  \&amp;\longrightarrow&amp;
                  Spin(8)
                  \\\
                  \\big\downarrow &amp;&amp; \big\downarrow
                  \\\
                  Sp(2) \cdot Sp(1)
                  \&amp;\longrightarrow&amp;
                  SO(8)
                  }
          %p
            with the horizontal maps being
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+homomorphisms"} group homomorphisms
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin%288%29"} Spin(8)
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SO%288%29"} SO(8)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
            projection and the right morphism the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+cover"} double cover
            morphism that defines the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+group"} spin group
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#CadekVanzura97"} Čadek-Vanžura 97, p. 4
          %h3#lift_to_
            Lift to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Sp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp(n) \times Sp(1)
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#MarchiafavaRomani76"}> Marchiafava-Romani 76
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Salamon82"} Salamon 82, around Def. 2.1
          %p (…)
          %p
            %br/
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#SO4
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi Sp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp(1)\cdot Sp(1)
            is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SO(4)
          %p
            The case of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi Sp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp(n)\cdot Sp(1)
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 1
            is special, as in this case the canonical inclusion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi Sp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi SO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 4
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp(n)\cdot Sp(1) \hookrightarrow SO(4n)
            becomes an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi Sp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi SO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Sp(1)\cdot Sp(1)
                  \\;\simeq\;
                  SO(4)
          %p
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+orthogonal+group"} special orthogonal group
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SO%284%29"} SO(4)
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:CompatibilityDiagram"} (2)
            now exhibits at the top the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exceptional+isomorphism"} exceptional isomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Sp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp(1) \times Sp(1) \simeq
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin%284%29"} Spin(4)
            (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "Spin4#ExceptionalIsomorphisms"} there
          %p In summary:
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              There is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groups"} Lie groups
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi q
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi q
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo ↦
                            %msub
                              %mi q
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ⋅
                            %mi x
                            %mo ⋅
                            %msub
                              %mover
                                %mi q
                                %mo ¯
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Sp
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ×
                            %mi Sp
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %mi Spin
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 4
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Sp
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ⋅
                            %mi Sp
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %mi SO
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 4
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    ( q_1, q_2 )
                    \&amp;\mapsto&amp;
                    (x \mapsto q_1 \cdot x \cdot \overline{q}_2)
                    \\\
                    Sp(1) \times Sp(1)
                    \&amp;\overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    Spin(4)
                    \\\
                    \\big\downarrow
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\big\downarrow
                    \\\
                    Sp(1)\cdot Sp(1)
                    \&amp;\overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    SO(4)
                    }
            %p where
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  in the top left we have
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sp%281%29"} Sp(1)
                  \=
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin%283%29"} Spin(3)
              %li
                %p
                  in the top right we have
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin%284%29"} Spin(4)
              %li
                %p
                  in the bottom left we have
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sp%28n%29.Sp%281%29"} Sp(1).Sp(1)
              %li
                %p
                  in the bottom right we have
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SO%284%29"} SO(4)
              %li
                %p
                  the horizontal morphism assigns the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjugation+action"} conjugation action
                  of unit
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternions"} quaternions
              %li
                %p
                  the right vertical morphism is the defining
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+cover"} double cover
              %li
                %p
                  the left vertical morphism is the defining
                  = succeed "-projection." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+group"} quotient group
          %p
            %br/
          %h3#Spinc
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(n)\cdot Spin(2)
            is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Spin
                    %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin^c(n)
          #SpinnSpin2IsSpinc.num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi Sp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp(n) \cdot Sp(2)
              in Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Spinn1Spinn2"}
              is the group otherwise known as
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin%5Ec"} spin^c(n)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi Spin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi Spin
                      %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Spin(n)\cdot Spin(2)
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    Spin^c(n)
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is due to the identification of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+cover"} double cover
              by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin%282%29"} Spin(2)
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SO%282%29"} SO(2)
              with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+Hopf+fibration"} real Hopf fibration
              (
              %a{:href => "Spin2#Spin2OverSO2IsRealHopfFibration"}> this Prop
              ), which identifies
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(2) \simeq U(1)
              compatible with the subgroupinclusion of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_2
          %p
            (See also e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Gompf97"} Gompf 97, p. 2
          %h3#Triality Triality
          #Spin3DotSpin5SubgroupsInSO8.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin%285%29.Spin%283%29"}> Spin(5).Spin(3)
                \-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroups"} subgroups
                in
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SO%288%29"} SO(8)
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+product+group"} direct product group
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SO%283%29"} SO(3)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ×
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \times
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SO%285%29"} SO(5)
              together with the groups
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sp%282%29.Sp%281%29"} Sp(2).Sp(1)
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Sp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mi Sp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp(1) \cdot Sp(2)
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SO%288%29"} SO(8)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjugacy+classes+of+subgroups"} conjugacy classes
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroups"} subgroups
              inside
